,"section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:64dfd9f50af53460b393574c80edee7bd6501c80012bdf401f9510e3649489aa","file":"preprints/Compatibility-entropy-and-the-spectrum-of-a-Thorp-sweep-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":53,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"34b59dc6a2e797f5e088754865cc34ec48d8c323c1e2e52ca2db4138dfe84e85","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Compatibility-entropy-and-the-spectrum-of-a-Thorp-sweep-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:64dfd9f50af53460b393574c80edee7bd6501c80012bdf401f9510e3649489aa","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Compatibility-entropy-and-the-spectrum-of-a-Thorp-sweep-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L53"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:intro-consequences}\nFor every nontrivial $\\lambda\\vdash n$ and $1\\le r\\le D_\\lambda$,\n\\[\n s_r(T_{n,\\lambda})\\le(16D_\\lambda r)^{-1/(2p_*)}.\n\\]\nIf $s_j(T_n)$ denotes the full regular singular list, including all multiplicities and zeros, then\n\\[\n s_j(T_n)\\le j^{-1/(2p_*)}\\qquad(1\\le j\\le n!).\n\\]\nThe constant singular value is the first value. The physical Thorp chain has worst-start $1/4$ mixing time $\\Theta(d)$; more precisely its lower bound is $2d-O(1)$. For every fixed integer $M>p_*$, the worst-start total-variation distance after $Md$ physical shuffles tends to zero as $d\\to\\infty$."}
